Error: Jet.ServiceImportOutsideCore: `source_key` imports a `jet.build` service, which only Core declares
  --> Tests/UI/service_import_outside_core.jet:2:48
    |
  2 | #Import(jet.build, symbol: "Build.source_key") source_key: fn(b: Build) -> String Never!
    |                                                ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The compiler and build host answer each `jet.build` symbol for the declaration Core writes for it; the provider, not a program, decides which services exist and where they run.
 Fix: Call the Core function or method that declares this service, such as `core.build` or `core.compiler`.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ServiceImportOutsideCore
